{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/814148-question-about-soak-from-an-st-perspective","id":814148,"title":"Question about Soak from an ST perspective","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-22T08:36:14-08:00","id":814148,"title":"Question about Soak from an ST perspective","content":"How do yall deal with Soak cause I always end up running into situations where the Soak of my players is too high for me to harm them or vice versa? Is it supposed to lower after a certain number of hits or is there something I'm missing? I don't know but any help would be appreciated.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11076-warkarx13","name":"Warkarx13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T09:36:33-08:00","id":814187,"title":"","content":"There are some creatures or circumstances that deal unsoakable damage. Gyuki for instance can attack a players shadow rather than the players themselves and thus deal damage that cannot be soaked. As can some Purviews, for instance the Ice Purview Soak doesn't decrease per se, but the DVs may (see Onslaught Penalty), which in turn allows for more dice to be taken over. Of course, more dice are somewhat neglectable around mid-Demigod (unless its from appropriately leveled Arete or differences in skill), given that you deal with characters that have a lot of soak. But if they do, then this is kind of their thing - take huge amounts of punishment without even a flinch. But if you want to make ir more challenging, buff up your enemies Epic Strength (and, possibly, Epic Dexterity, but be careful with that) and look into the Sun, Fire, Frost and possibly Illusion Purview. <br /> <br /> Also, Epic Intelligence can help, should you have the &quot;Fight with your head&quot; Knack. This allows you to pretty much negate any soak a character has, but only for the NPC who uses that Knack on him or her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T14:10:56-08:00","id":814446,"title":"","content":"Your NPC's need more Epic Strength to beat the Epic Stamina of PC's. I'm honestly surprised that <i>soak</i> is your problem, not DV. With Untouchable Opponent, DV is almost always the game-breaker.<br /> <br /> There are tons of weapons that do Piercing damage. Aggravated damage is hard to soak, even <i>with</i> Epic Stamina. Soak is not a solid defense in Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T16:56:22-08:00","id":814541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/814148-question-about-soak-from-an-st-perspective?p=814446#post814446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your NPC's need more Epic Strength to beat the Epic Stamina of PC's. I'm honestly surprised that <i>soak</i> is your problem, not DV. With Untouchable Opponent, DV is almost always the game-breaker.<br /> <br /> There are tons of weapons that do Piercing damage. Aggravated damage is hard to soak, even <i>with</i> Epic Stamina. Soak is not a solid defense in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> The reason I haven't had an issue with DV yet is because my players don't focus on it too often and I tend to get lucky when it comes to hitting them, I guess. Also their DVs don't matter half the time because I have a Son of Odin who is a Epic Strength and Epic Stamina whore who acts as the meatsheild for the other players.<br /> \u200b<br /> That said, I appreciate the advice yall have given me so far. My players and I are relatively new to scion, although the JSR stuff is a godsend, so I will be sure to look into these things. Although it sounds like I've just been too easy on them based on what I've heard so far. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11076,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11076-warkarx13","user":"Warkarx13","date":". 01-22-2016, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11076-warkarx13","name":"Warkarx13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}